diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index b3424ea1b..282994024 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@ Bugs
 - Fix :func:`moabb.analysis.plotting.summary_plot` raising ``ValueError: The truth value of a Series is ambiguous`` when two pipeline names shorten to the same first word, such as ``Tangent Space LR`` and ``Tangent Space SVM Grid`` from ``pipelines/``. It now keeps the full names and logs a warning, the same as ``analyze`` already does (by `Iain`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Gao2026` returning EEG amplitudes 256 times too small. The loader divided every EEG channel by 256, assuming the BDF header's 16-bit digital range (-32768..32767) was wrong for 24-bit data. It is not: each released file stores values within that range and sets its physical range to its own largest sample (10 mV to 375 mV across the 125 recordings), so MNE's header calibration already gives the correct amplitudes (median channel SD about 9 µV at 1-40 Hz, Fp1/Fp2 blinks about 250 µV, occipital visual evoked responses about 10 µV; 0.03 µV, 1 µV and 0.04 µV after the division). Adds a regression test on a synthetic BDF stored the same way (:gh:`1330` by `Adam Rolander`_).
 - Fix the evaluations returning each result several times when datasets share a processing pipeline (e.g. :class:`~moabb.datasets.fake.FakeDataset` instances that differ only in their channels): ``process`` collected the whole results group of the pipeline for every dataset, instead of the rows of that dataset (:gh:`1305` by `Quentin Barthelemy`_).
-- Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.HefmiIch2025` returning subjects made of other people's sessions. The figshare file names carry no subject (``1_epo.mat``, ``2_epo.mat``, ``3_epo.mat``), and the loader grouped the EEG epoch files by figshare upload order, starting a new subject at every ``1_epo.mat``: 23 of its 37 subjects mixed sessions of two to four people, 31 of the 37 people were split over two or three subjects, and subjects had up to 6 sessions. Subjects and sessions now follow the depositor's folders, which the ``folder_structure`` of the figshare record (article 28955456, version 4) gives for every file and which the article's ZIP uses: subjects 1-17 are ``epo_data/Normals/EEG/subject1`` to ``subject17`` (healthy controls), subjects 18-37 are ``epo_data/Patients/EEG/subject1`` to ``subject20`` (ICH patients), and session ``str(k - 1)`` is the file ``<k>_epo.mat``: 98 sessions (1-3 per subject, consecutive runs of one visit) and 2,940 trials instead of the 3,330 the metadata declared. The creation times in the files' MAT headers agree with these folders. The loader ships the mapping with the size and MD5 of every file, checks each file against them, and stores the files under the depositor's paths; the NEMAR deposit ``nm000347``, which files the epochs under the former subjects, is no longer declared. **Delete cached HefmiIch2025 epochs and saved results computed before this fix and recompute them:** MOABB has no per-dataset cache version, so a cache built with the former grouping is otherwise reused as is. The previously downloaded ``subNN_k_epo.mat`` files and ``manifest.json`` in ``MNE-hefmiich2025-data`` are no longer read and can be deleted (:gh:`1326` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.HefmiIch2025` returning subjects made of other people's sessions. The figshare file names carry no subject (``1_epo.mat``, ``2_epo.mat``, ``3_epo.mat``), and the loader grouped the EEG epoch files by figshare upload order, starting a new subject at every ``1_epo.mat``: 23 of its 37 subjects mixed sessions of two to four people, 31 of the 37 people were split over two or three subjects, and subjects had up to 6 sessions. Subjects and sessions now follow the depositor's folders, which the ``folder_structure`` of the figshare record (article 28955456, version 4) gives for every file and which the article's ZIP uses: subjects 1-17 are ``epo_data/Normals/EEG/subject1`` to ``subject17`` (healthy controls), subjects 18-37 are ``epo_data/Patients/EEG/subject1`` to ``subject20`` (ICH patients), and session ``str(k - 1)`` is the file ``<k>_epo.mat``: 98 sessions (1-3 per subject, consecutive runs of one visit) and 2,940 trials instead of the 3,330 the metadata declared. The creation times in the files' MAT headers agree with these folders. The loader ships the mapping with the size and MD5 of every file, checks each file against them, and stores the files under the depositor's paths; the NEMAR deposit ``nm000347`` (v1.0.5) has been re-filed under the same depositor folders (``sub-01``..``sub-37``) and serves them. **Delete cached HefmiIch2025 epochs and saved results computed before this fix and recompute them:** MOABB has no per-dataset cache version, so a cache built with the former grouping is otherwise reused as is. The previously downloaded ``subNN_k_epo.mat`` files and ``manifest.json`` in ``MNE-hefmiich2025-data`` are no longer read and can be deleted (:gh:`1326` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix the evaluations training and scoring filter-bank pipelines on the first band only: since 1.4.0 (:gh:`774`), :class:`moabb.evaluations.base.BaseEvaluation` passed ``get_data`` the processing pipeline of the first filter alone, so with :class:`moabb.paradigms.FilterBankLeftRightImagery`, :class:`moabb.paradigms.FilterBankMotorImagery` or :class:`moabb.paradigms.FilterBankSSVEP` the data reaching an array pipeline had one band instead of one per filter (shape ``(n_trials, n_channels, n_times, 1)``). FBCSP and the SSVEP MDM, TS + LR and TS + SVM pipelines scored well below their published values (Nakanishi2015 SSVEP TS + LR 0.26 instead of 0.87; with every band, 0.89). Epoch-based pipelines (TRCA, TDCA, CCA, deep learning) were not affected. Results of filter-bank pipelines computed with MOABB 1.4.0 to 1.7.2 must be recomputed (:gh:`1291` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.BNCI2015_004` names its five mental tasks again (word association, mental subtraction, spatial navigation, right hand and feet imagery, coded 1-5 as in the .mat files) and epochs the imagery period [3, 10] s; since v1.5 the events were those of another dataset, the window covered the fixation cross, and :class:`moabb.paradigms.MotorImagery` rejected the dataset (:gh:`1323` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_)
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Wang2016` lists all 35 subjects (S35.mat was never loaded) (:gh:`1322` by `Rızgar Ozan`_, merged in :gh:`1323`)
